// The Reid & Nahon standard tests' gravity, shared by the three case sims.
//
// The golden runs they are overlaid on were made with the washout repo's
// default, g = 9.81 m/s^2; `Classical` defaults to standard gravity, 9.80665.
// The difference is small, but it is in every tilt angle (asin(a/g)) and in the
// -g inside `sf`, so it would be a real, if tiny, disagreement that has nothing
// to do with the model.
//
// It lives in TWO settings: `Classical` does not flow its `grav` down into
// `TiltCalc`, whose `G` has its own default. They agree only because both
// defaults happen to be the same number. `grav` is a record, and an override
// addresses one field of it at a time (SE0460); only Z is nonzero.
wash.grav.z     = 9.81 (m/s^2);
wash.tiltCalc.G = 9.81 (m/s^2);
